# HTML tags

## Line breaks

  First line
  second line
  third line
  fourth line
  fifth.

## Keys and marks

  Press `Ctrl`+`C` to copy, or `Page Down` to
  move on.

  Some text is marked as found, even in bold.

  A <kbd>key that never closes stays as
  source.

## Details

  <details>
  <summary>A summary with <kbd>Esc</kbd></summary>

  The content is Markdown, as GitHub shows it:

  - one
  - two

  </details>

  <details><summary>Written on one line</summary>The content &amp; its
  <b>tags</b> are plain text.</details>

  <details>

  Without a summary, the block is called
  Details.

  </details>

  - A list item

    <details>
    <summary>Inside a list</summary>

    Content in the list.

    </details>

  > <details>
  > <summary>Inside a quote</summary>
  >
  > Content in the quote.
  >
  > </details>

## Other tags

  Text with <b>bold</b> and <span>a
  span</span> stays as source.

  <div>
  A div block stays as source.
  </div>

  <details>
  <summary>Never closed</summary>

  Runs to the end of the document.
